Sweep the canonical corpus: every body compact with its record, the Scala gate-pinned

Dev accepted, on 2026-10-21, "sweeping the rest of the canonical corpus in one pass: every remaining
main definition and the staged dreams and service definitions compacted with their records, Scala
byte-identical and gate-pinned, the example domains left out."

The sweep compacts 132 definitions — the 108 main definitions other than the authored-ahead
BodyElement and ActorAspect, which keep their frozen surfaces, and the 24 staged dreams and service
definitions — against the canonical identity ontology and HostBindings: 55 JSON files change, 50
drake surfaces are re-emitted, 58 definitions carry a record. The example domains stay out. Two
first runs of the sweep taught the compact form three rules it now keeps. A HOST LEAF KEEPS THE
AUTHOR'S SPELLING: the compact form never writes a binding's identity into a definition and never
shortens one, since the vocabulary is the target's; the previous compact shortened host names, so eleven
definition-backed Scala files regenerate: the host imports gained at 0b8fc03 (`import java.nio.file.Files`,
`import org.evrete.api.ActivationMode`) revert, and Decoder, Encoder and Generated are spelled in full
where a host name shadows them. AN IDENTITY IS SHORTENED ONLY
WHEN ITS SIMPLE NAME IS UNIQUE ACROSS THE ONTOLOGY AND THE VOCABULARY, so a reader holding just the
file's record finds it unambiguous and a target table does not capture it — Decoder and Encoder in
the Dracon domain stay in full — with the draco.rete wrap types the exception, bare as they always
were, since their bare name is their realization. AN ANCHOR'S TYPE PARAMETERS FOLLOW THE ANCHOR'S
CONVENTION, bare in the own package and in full elsewhere, never the record's short form: Nominal
still derives `Primal(draco.drake.Text)`.

Two more corrections the sweep forced. The engine's loader resolved a recorded definition through
its record for EVERY caller, so DomainBuilder and the companions disagreed about one definition and
TransformBinding.matches refused the held GenDrake; the record is now read only during a generation.
The hand-written draco.Generated bootstrap shadows draco.dreams.editor.Generated through
`import draco._`, so it joins HostBindings' engine bindings — a host realization the compact form
must not shorten past — and KnowledgeService's binding names org.evrete, where the class is.

GenDrakeTest moves one pin to the swept spelling: Emission's parameter says Text and its record
names draco.drake.Text, the anchor unchanged. ResolutionRecordTest's second test now covers the
whole main corpus: unscoped generation equals scoped generation for every definition, and the
pinned file for every definition with a file of its own.

Probe on the compiled engine from a clean restore: the sweep, then every definition verified —
unscoped equals scoped equals pinned for all 132 and both sealed families — the whole main and mods
tree compiled, and 31 suites, 775 passed, zero failed or aborted, every headline unchanged, pending
mods actors 0. No test or corpus type added.

Dev's first full gate failed one test (848 of 849): DomainLineTest pinned the bootstrap spelling of
three swept bodies — Surface, DomainLine and DomainLineOf saying draco.drake.Text — as GenDrakeTest
had; its pins now say Text with each record naming draco.drake.Text, the anchor unchanged. An
all-suites probe without the test resources on the loader's roots also failed three scenario tests,
a probe artifact Dev's run did not show.

Gate: Dev's second full sbt run on 2026-10-21, pasted: 849 tests / 60 suites, zero failed, canceled,
ignored or pending tests, zero aborted suites; every report-only headline unchanged; pending mods
actors 0 in the file-only log. Committed and pushed by Dev.

